  "conclusion": "Qwen3-8B is the strongest strict baseline tested, but its gain over Qwen3-4B is marginal and it is not production-ready. It adds four contract-valid outputs and three strict correct decisions, while raw decision accuracy rises by only one case and accepted correction texts remain 17/27. With roughly twice the weight bytes, 45% higher mean latency, and about 43% lower request-latency throughput than 4B, keep Qwen3-4B as the efficient first LoRA candidate and Qwen3-8B as a scaling reference. Use separate training data to teach the judgment contract, minimal corrections, and Unicode edit offsets."
